From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:58:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] 
 mm-filemap-convert-fault-and-readahead-logic-to-use-vma_flags_t-fix-fix

make random_read const, per Lorenzo

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes (ARM) <ljs@kernel.org>
---
 mm/filemap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/filemap.c b/mm/filemap.c
index 1500aec89f8cf..93db8fc60ae0a 100644
--- a/mm/filemap.c
+++ b/mm/filemap.c
@@ -3409,7 +3409,7 @@ static struct file *do_sync_mmap_readahead(struct vm_fault *vmf)
 
 	if (force_thp_readahead) {
 		unsigned long folio_nr_pages = 1UL << thp_order;
-		bool random_read = vma_test(vma, VMA_RAND_READ_BIT);
+		const bool random_read = vma_test(vma, VMA_RAND_READ_BIT);
 
 		fpin = maybe_unlock_mmap_for_io(vmf, fpin);
 		ractl._index &= ~(folio_nr_pages - 1);
-- 
2.47.3

